    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the policy side, but I'm worried about the \"structural certainty\" part. Some analysts are pointing to the massive capital requirements for grid upgrades, the volatility in critical mineral markets like lithium and cobalt, and the sheer scale of inflation that comes with replacing trillions in existing infrastructure. Aren't those massive economic hurdles enough to make the whole \"inevitability\" narrative look a bit too optimistic/speculative?",
